  "description": "On a table-type recordset over F: read Index; assign Index in turn IX_N, ix_n, \" IX_N\", \"IX_N \", PrimaryKey, PK_F, \"\", Null, Long 0, NoSuch and F, reading Index back, then MoveFirst and reading ID and N after each. Then on a dynaset, a snapshot and a forward-only recordset over F: read Index, assign PK_F, read Index. Asks the Index spellings accepted (case, spaces, the default primary-key name), the value read back, the order that results, and which recordset types have the property. The fixture copy is opened read-only.",
